---
title: Yorkshire puddings
servings: 6
yield: 12 puddings
tags: [british, vegetarian, christmas, holiday, winter]
cuisine: british
time: 30 minutes
source: Amazing Yorkies by Jamie Oliver, https://www.jamieoliver.com/recipes/eggs/amazing-yorkies/
---

Heat the oven to 225°C (425°F).

Pour 1 cm of @vegetable oil{} into each cup of a #12-cup muffin tin{}. Put the tin in the oven ~{10-15%minutes} until the oil is very hot.

Meanwhile, beat the @eggs{2}(large), @all-purpose flour{100%g}, @milk{100%ml} and a pinch each of @salt{} and @black pepper{} in a #jug{} until smooth.

Take the tin out carefully and pour the batter evenly into the cups.

Bake ~{12-15%minutes} until risen and golden. Keep the oven door shut until then.

> The oil has to be smoking hot when the batter goes in; that is what makes them rise.
